{
  "_comment": "A lens is a subject whose own history a story can draw Beginnings from (T-0076, docs/decisions.md). Matched by whole words in the object's Title, by sub-genre or row, or by an object id listed under include, rule-based, so the editor can read and change it. A story's row can be shared by many subjects; the lens is what the story is about. Rule: per lens, the most recent three linked objects dated before the story's origin; a provisional row needs at least three in all, otherwise it shows its origin alone. A lens with fewer than three linked objects is a gap to fill through the staging workbook. `story_terms` (whole words, any case) and `story_terms_cs` (whole words, exact case) are what the story's own text must contain before a lens may be applied to it; a lens with no support in the story is dropped (T-0079).",
